{"duration_api_ms":94494,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"3db5ebcf-4536-4fdd-85c1-d322ebd6e4c1","total_cost_usd":0.2764358,"usage":{"input_tokens":24,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23044,"cache_read_input_tokens":485159,"output_tokens":8718,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2836},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23044,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1855,"cache_read_input_tokens":45494,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1881},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":24,"outputTokens":8718,"cacheReadInputTokens":485159,"cacheCreationInputTokens":23044,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2764358,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2836,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":13,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"On node1, deployed inventory-api as a systemd-managed service (inventory-api.service) with OOMScoreAdjust=-1000, enabled and running on port 8080 via $NODE_IP. Verified the kernel's global OOM killer, when driven out of memory by an unprotected memory-hog process (oom_score_adj=0), selects and kills the hog while inventory-api keeps serving without interruption (same PID before/after). Confirmed this behavior both before and after a full node reboot, and proved the reboot actually occurred via a changed boot_id and fresh uptime.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 baseline: Ubuntu 24.04, 1.9GiB RAM, no swap, python3 available\",\"Wrote /usr/local/bin/inventory-api.py, a threaded HTTP JSON service on port 8080\",\"Created /etc/systemd/system/inventory-api.service with OOMScoreAdjust=-1000, Restart=always, enabled at boot\",\"Wrote /usr/local/bin/memory-hog.py, an unbounded memory-consuming script\",\"Started inventory-api and verified active state, PID, oom_score_adj=-1000, and successful curl\",\"Launched memory-hog as a transient systemd unit (memory-hog.service) with default oom_score_adj=0\",\"Polled memory usage and dmesg until the kernel's global OOM killer fired\",\"Confirmed dmesg shows 'Out of memory: Killed process ... (python3) ... oom_score_adj:0' targeting the hog, while inventory-api remained active with unchanged PID and uptime growing\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and service health baseline\",\"Issued 'sudo -n systemctl reboot' on node1; acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again\",\"Verified boot_id changed and uptime reflects a fresh boot\",\"Verified inventory-api auto-started (enabled), correct oom_score_adj=-1000, and served a request post-reboot\",\"Re-ran the memory-hog OOM scenario post-reboot to confirm the protection persists across restart: kernel again killed the hog, inventory-api stayed active throughout\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"inventory-api runs as a managed (systemd) service on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a1b20ec721ad438f\"],\"summary\":\"Unit created, enabled, active; MainPID reported by systemctl; curl returns valid JSON response\"},{\"requirement\":\"inventory-api is protected from the OOM killer (oom_score_adj=-1000)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a1b20ec721ad438f\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl show reports OOMScoreAdjust=-1000 and /proc/<pid>/oom_score_adj confirms -1000\"},{\"requirement\":\"Under real system memory pressure, the kernel OOM killer stops the memory-hog process, not inventory-api\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0cd710d370df45c8\",\"cmd-c3c6f2b8a13d4e86\"],\"summary\":\"Memory hog launched with oom_score_adj=0; dmesg shows 'Out of memory: Killed process 1315 (python3) ... oom_score_adj:0'; inventory-api (pid 1285) remained active the entire time with growing uptime and a successful curl response after the kill; free -h shows memory reclaimed\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline and boot identity capture on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f58c72a08e564f18\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 1e0cb179-d384-41f8-aa25-9390b31eec45, confirmed inventory-api active+enabled and serving via curl\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledgement returns before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a5be39b631174629\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot issued and returned exit_code 0 before the node disconnected\"},{\"requirement\":\"Proof of changed boot identity after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0673b14b959d48db\",\"cmd-36bd4d6e86df4d4a\"],\"summary\":\"Immediate poll failed with connection reset (node down), next poll succeeded with new boot_id d409655a-9797-475d-a310-6e7931adf86d, differing from the pre-restart value\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of inventory-api and re-verification of OOM protection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3099e5d892d942ee\"],\"summary\":\"Fresh uptime confirms new boot; inventory-api active/enabled with new PID 649, oom_score_adj=-1000, serving curl; re-ran the memory-hog scenario post-reboot and dmesg again shows the kernel killing the unprotected hog (pid 893) while inventory-api (pid 649) stayed active and kept serving throughout\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1, deployed inventory-api as a systemd-managed service (inventory-api.service) with OOMScoreAdjust=-1000, enabled and running on port 8080 via $NODE_IP. Verified the kernel's global OOM killer, when driven out of memory by an unprotected memory-hog process (oom_score_adj=0), selects and kills the hog while inventory-api keeps serving without interruption (same PID before/after). Confirmed this behavior both before and after a full node reboot, and proved the reboot actually occurred via a changed boot_id and fresh uptime.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 baseline: Ubuntu 24.04, 1.9GiB RAM, no swap, python3 available","Wrote /usr/local/bin/inventory-api.py, a threaded HTTP JSON service on port 8080","Created /etc/systemd/system/inventory-api.service with OOMScoreAdjust=-1000, Restart=always, enabled at boot","Wrote /usr/local/bin/memory-hog.py, an unbounded memory-consuming script","Started inventory-api and verified active state, PID, oom_score_adj=-1000, and successful curl","Launched memory-hog as a transient systemd unit (memory-hog.service) with default oom_score_adj=0","Polled memory usage and dmesg until the kernel's global OOM killer fired","Confirmed dmesg shows 'Out of memory: Killed process ... (python3) ... oom_score_adj:0' targeting the hog, while inventory-api remained active with unchanged PID and uptime growing","Captured pre-restart boot_id and service health baseline","Issued 'sudo -n systemctl reboot' on node1; acknowledgement returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again","Verified boot_id changed and uptime reflects a fresh boot","Verified inventory-api auto-started (enabled), correct oom_score_adj=-1000, and served a request post-reboot","Re-ran the memory-hog OOM scenario post-reboot to confirm the protection persists across restart: kernel again killed the hog, inventory-api stayed active throughout"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"inventory-api runs as a managed (systemd) service on node1","command_ids":["cmd-a1b20ec721ad438f"],"summary":"Unit created, enabled, active; MainPID reported by systemctl; curl returns valid JSON response"},{"requirement":"inventory-api is protected from the OOM killer (oom_score_adj=-1000)","command_ids":["cmd-a1b20ec721ad438f"],"summary":"systemctl show reports OOMScoreAdjust=-1000 and /proc/<pid>/oom_score_adj confirms -1000"},{"requirement":"Under real system memory pressure, the kernel OOM killer stops the memory-hog process, not inventory-api","command_ids":["cmd-0cd710d370df45c8","cmd-c3c6f2b8a13d4e86"],"summary":"Memory hog launched with oom_score_adj=0; dmesg shows 'Out of memory: Killed process 1315 (python3) ... oom_score_adj:0'; inventory-api (pid 1285) remained active the entire time with growing uptime and a successful curl response after the kill; free -h shows memory reclaimed"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline and boot identity capture on node1","command_ids":["cmd-f58c72a08e564f18"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 1e0cb179-d384-41f8-aa25-9390b31eec45, confirmed inventory-api active+enabled and serving via curl"},{"requirement":"Node1 restart acknowledgement returns before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-a5be39b631174629"],"summary":"systemctl reboot issued and returned exit_code 0 before the node disconnected"},{"requirement":"Proof of changed boot identity after restart","command_ids":["cmd-0673b14b959d48db","cmd-36bd4d6e86df4d4a"],"summary":"Immediate poll failed with connection reset (node down), next poll succeeded with new boot_id d409655a-9797-475d-a310-6e7931adf86d, differing from the pre-restart value"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of inventory-api and re-verification of OOM protection","command_ids":["cmd-3099e5d892d942ee"],"summary":"Fresh uptime confirms new boot; inventory-api active/enabled with new PID 649, oom_score_adj=-1000, serving curl; re-ran the memory-hog scenario post-reboot and dmesg again shows the kernel killing the unprotected hog (pid 893) while inventory-api (pid 649) stayed active and kept serving throughout"}]},"ttft_ms":25617,"type":"result","duration_ms":114385,"uuid":"63b9e93b-5fb8-4cee-8470-01c49c34d1cc","ttft_stream_ms":4113,"time_to_request_ms":161